{"step_index":180,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T12:31:33Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 2 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. possible to show me all your reasoning and formuale in the apps? so that i can have more confident on u\n2. can i open this apps in my other deivce? means can you publish it online as a pwa?\n3. i have a github account,. i think you have access to it no? you hlped me push other git already\n4. install the \" GitHub CLI \" to your skill\n5. i would like to use something that u can automate in the future, and please guide me step by step\n6. hostname?\n7. done\n8. help me deploy to streamlit as well\n9. good success already. but now I want to have one function that remember the stock and the price I’ve bought\n10. provide me more features that can make this apps better . search across the network. and all the explanation tutorials those keep it inside a dropdown will do\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n1. Outstanding User Requests\n- \"provide me more features that can make this apps better . search across the network. and all the explanation tutorials those keep it inside a dropdown will do\" -> Status: IMPLEMENTATION. (Code for Plotly charts, caching, CSV export, scoring system, and consolidated dropdowns was just written, committed, and pushed to GitHub. The next agent just needs to notify the user of these new features).\n\n2. User Knowledge\n- Target Trading Strategies: Based on the books \"海龟交易法则\" (Way of the Turtle) and \"Jack Investment\" (a Malaysian stock trading influencer).\n- App Capabilities: Must act as a real-time stock screener for Malaysia and US stocks. Provide Technical Analysis (TA), Take Profit (TP), Cut Loss (CL), and Entry Price.\n- Ticker Resolution: User prefers typing company names (e.g., \"SUNCON\") instead of exact Yahoo Finance tickers (`5263.KL`).\n- Custom Entries: User tracks existing positions using the syntax `TICKER@PRICE` (e.g., `SUNCON@2.50`). The app must evaluate if they should HOLD, TAKE PROFIT, or SELL based on this price.\n- Explanations: Wanted explanations of the \"1:1.5 RR Target\" and strategy rules built directly into the app UI, written in Mandarin but retaining English terms. User requested all tutorials be consolidated into a dropdown.\n- Deployment: User wanted to access the app on other devices (PWA). They authenticated the GitHub CLI (`gh`) locally. The repository is published at `https://github.com/ngwaijian/stock-screener`.\n- Portfolio Memory: User requested a function to \"remember the stock and the price I’ve bought\".\n\n3. Work Accomplished\n- Read and extracted strategy rules from \"10_JACK INVESTMENT.pdf\".\n- Created `stock_screener.py` using Streamlit, `yfinance`, and `pandas`.\n- Implemented Yahoo Finance Search API integration to automatically resolve user-friendly company names to exact ticker symbols.\n- Added a `portfolio.json` save feature to persist the user's entered tickers and `@price` positions locally/in-session.\n- Built a two-tab interface: \"Discovery Scanner\" (auto-scans a hardcoded list of 30 top US and 30 top MY stocks for fresh setups) and \"My Portfolio\" (tracks specific user stocks).\n- Deployed the application by initializing a local Git repo and pushing it to `https://github.com/ngwaijian/stock-screener`.\n- In response to the most recent feature request, successfully researched web suggestions, installed `plotly`, rewrote `stock_screener.py` to add interactive candlestick charts, data caching, CSV export, a 5-point Technical Score, and a consolidated tutorial expander. Committed and pushed these updates to GitHub.\n\n4. Model Knowledge\n- **Pandas 3.0+ Deprecation:** `Styler.applymap()` is deprecated and removed in Pandas >= 3.0. Use `Styler.map()` instead. This caused a runtime error previously.\n- **Yfinance MultiIndex Issue:** In newer `yfinance` versions, `yf.download` for a single ticker returns columns as a `MultiIndex` (e.g., `('Close', 'AAPL')`). This causes Series comparison errors. Fix used: `if isinstance(df.columns, pd.MultiIndex): df.columns = df.columns.droplevel(1)`.\n- **Jack Investment Strategy:** Mid-to-short-term swing trading. \n  - *Buy rules:* Uptrend (Close > EMA30), Consolidation Box (20-day high-low diff < 20%), Breakout (Close > High20), Volume Surge (Vol > 1.2x Vol20 avg), Strong close (Upper half of candle).\n  - *CL:* 20-day Low * 0.98 (2% buffer below support).\n  - *TP:* Entry + (Entry - CL) * 1.5 (1:1.5 Risk-Reward ratio).\n- **Turtle Trading Strategy:** System 1 (20-day breakout). CL = Entry - 2*ATR20. TP = Trailing stop below 10-day Low.\n\n5. Files and Code\n- `C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1/stock_screener.py` (Edited heavily): Core Streamlit application. Contains the dual-strategy analysis functions, Plotly charting, Yahoo API ticker resolution, caching, and UI layout.\n- `C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1/requirements.txt` (Edited): Dependencies `streamlit`, `yfinance`, `pandas`, `numpy`, `requests`, `plotly`.\n- `C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1/portfolio.json` (Created): Stores the serialized dictionary of the user's saved tickers.\n- `w:/My Drive/ZLibrary/02_To Read/2026/10_JACK INVESTMENT.pdf` (Viewed): The source material for the Jack Investment strategy.\n\n6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Current Work:** I just pushed the final batch of major feature enhancements (Interactive Plotly charts, caching, CSV downloading, Technical Scoring, and the consolidated Tutorial dropdown) to the user's GitHub repository.\n- **Next Step:** Notify the user that these new features have been successfully added and